# Common Beginner Mistakes

❌ Leaving

```cpp
str = nullptr;
```

instead of allocating an empty string.

---

❌ Forgetting

```cpp
+1
```

when allocating memory.

---

❌ Using

```cpp
delete
```

instead of

```cpp
delete[]
```

---

❌ Shallow Copy

```cpp
str = source.str;
```

---

❌ Forgetting to implement a destructor.

---

# Best Practices

- Always keep every object in a valid state.
- Every allocation must have exactly one matching delete.
- Prefer Deep Copy over Shallow Copy.
- Getter functions should usually be `const`.
- Return `const` pointers whenever possible.
- Understand memory ownership before writing classes.

